{
  "schema": 1,
  "description": "Goals (docs/goals.md, supabase/migrations/0009_goals.sql). 'periods': the first and last day of the period of 'horizon' that 'day' falls in (weeks start on Monday). 'parents': whether a goal of 'parent' can serve as the parent of a goal of 'child': the parent's horizon must be longer (year > month > week > day) and its period must overlap the child's. 'progress': a goal's progress from its mode, its status, the tasks that serve it (not deleted; dropped ones don't count) and the amounts logged on it (deleted ones don't count): 'done' mode is 1 of 1 when the goal is done; 'tasks' is the tasks done of those that count; 'number' is the sum of the amounts against the target. A done goal is hit with its fraction at 1; a dropped goal is never hit; otherwise hit means the fraction reached 1. 'fraction' is value / target, at most 1 and 0 when there is nothing to count. 'copy': last period's goals copied into the next period: every goal that wasn't dropped, open again, keeping its parent only when the parent's period overlaps the new one. 2026-09-18 is a Friday. 'pace': where an open goal stands against the share of its period gone by, the days before 'today' over the period's days (0 before it starts, 1 after it ends): dropped, hit, behind or on track. A goal counted by tasks or a number is on track while its fraction plus 0.05 reaches that share, and otherwise behind by the amount still missing to it, rounded up ('behind'). A done-or-not goal, or one with nothing to count, is behind once 0.7 of its period is gone, with no amount. 2026-10-01 is a Thursday. 'order': goals sorted for a rung, the ones behind first, then on track, then hit, then dropped, keeping their order within each. 'chain': what lights up when a goal is picked: the goal, every goal it feeds up the cascade and every goal that feeds it, however deep; a missing parent ends the climb and a loop is walked once. 'quick': the amount the quick log adds on a numeric goal: the latest positive amount logged by hand (by 'created', deleted ones skipped), or null when there is none.",
